   "text": "I read the drawing as a head-to-side-chain cyclic peptide. The thioether macrocycle runs from Cys to a chloroacetyl-capped Tyr, and each of the two squaramide arms carries a 4-(ethoxycarbonyl)phenylamino group.\n\n**Sequence, C-terminus to N-terminus as written in the SMILES:**\n- Gly-NH2, then Cys, whose sulfur is bridged through S-CH2-C(=O) to the N-terminal Tyr.\n- Leu, N-Me-norleucine, N-Me-norleucine.\n- Trp carrying N1-CH2COOH on the indole.\n- Dab, whose side-chain NH is attached to a squaramide.\n- Trp, then trans-4-hydroxy-Pro, then Leu.\n- Dap, whose \u03b2-NH is attached to a squaramide.\n- Pro, Asn, N-Me-Ala, and finally Tyr, which carries the thioacetyl cap.\n\n**Two readings I settled by counting:**\n- The long line from the top squaramide NH runs to a side chain with two CH2 groups after the \u03b1-carbon, so that residue is Dab (not Orn).\n- The two norleucine side chains each have four carbons, so they are butyl.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I worked out each centre from the wedges and hashes, and they all correspond to L-amino acids. Cys is R by CIP priority, and the 4-hydroxyproline is (2S,4R), i.e. trans.\n\nSMILES: NC(=O)CNC(=O)[C@@H]1CSCC(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](CNC2=C(Nc3ccc(C(=O)OCC)cc3)C(=O)C2=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N2C[C@H](O)C[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCNC2=C(Nc3ccc(C(=O)OCC)cc3)C(=O)C2=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cn(CC(=O)O)c3ccccc23)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCC)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CCCC)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N1"
